  "sourceNotes": "Chicken tikka is the base preparation from which chicken tikka masala is derived. Tikka (Hindi for small piece, from the Persian) refers to pieces of food marinated in spiced yogurt and cooked in a tandoor. Madhur Jaffrey, Madhur Jaffrey's Indian Cookery (BBC Books, 1982): tikka marinade technique. Served dry as a starter in British curry restaurants from the 1970s onwards.",
